        "body": "<!-- greptile_comment -->\n\n<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=107410293&amp;sig=4bf6323e04476eb945cd71d2497da5c3c5754b3fd0ea4d318b267942ad4a2fa6\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/-/switch-tenant?tenant=nero&amp;next=%2Frajnagani31%2Ffastapi%2Fpull%2F11&amp;utm_source=greptile_review&amp;utm_medium=github&amp;utm_campaign=view_in_greptile\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewInGreptileDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewInGreptile.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"View in Greptile\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewInGreptile.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 5/5</h2>\n\n<!-- greptile-impact-verdict --> The PR appears safe to merge, with the earlier non-blocking duplicate-upkeep concern still open.\n\n<h2>Findings</h2>\n\n1. <img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**Examples need duplicate upkeep** <a href=\"https://github.com/rajnagani31/FastAPI/pull/11#discussion_r4577659561\">\u25b6</a>\n\n<details open><summary><h3>Summary</h3></summary>\n\nThe PR adds three copied sets of Pydantic lessons. Since the previous review, it adds the seven files in `08_pydantic copy 3/`.\n\n- User and product examples show how typed fields shape model data.\n- Employee fields and decorator examples show checks and call order.\n- Validation examples check, transform, and calculate model values.\n- Nested examples place addresses and replies inside models.\n- Serialization examples format dates and print model data.\n- A settings example prints its defaults as JSON.\n</details>\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:5 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (3) \u00b7 Last reviewed commit: [\"test nero ai ai-engin\"](https://github.com/rajnagani31/fastapi/commit/f9f2ef8e861ec237900a34c908a71a97c69a1720) \u00b7 [Reviewed by Greptile](https://www.greptile.com/?utm_source=greptile_review&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=review_public&utm_content=rajnagani31/fastapi)</sub>\n\n<!-- /greptile_comment -->",
